{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe","id":1128540,"title":"What if? The Marvel Universe","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-13T12:21:41-07:00","id":1128540,"title":"What if? The Marvel Universe","content":"So anyone who knows Marvel knows one famous question. What if? So not to beat around the bush... <br /> <br /> What if the Marvel Universe was set in the Chronicles of Darkness?<br /> <br /> Part of why I'm asking is just that this is a fun conversation to have, but part of it is also that I've always wanted to do own take on a unified, coherent Marvel storyline. That motivation actually predates the MCU by several years. I also enjoy doing CofD crossovers, so it hit me that it would be interesting to try and blend the two together. Ironically, I'm not actually a huge comic hound, but I grew up on the Spiderman and X-Men animated series, so I'd also appreciate suggestions as to what to read and avoid.<br /> <br /> Just to lay some base rules, I'm totally open to people discussing multiple possibilities for who characters would be and how the world would work. Interpretations could range from obvious (most everyone is a Deviant, Doctor Strange is a Mage) to plausible (the Xavier Institue houses a variety of Proximi, Offspring, Fractals, Ghouls, and other demi-splats) to really out there (Peter Parker, Spider-Gwen, and Mike Morales make a Forsaken Pack with a Spider Totem that grants them powers). In my eyes, all of those are equally valid and worthy of discussion. <br /> <br /> So what do you think? What if the Marvel Universe took place in the Chronicles of Darkness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T12:29:20-07:00","id":1128543,"title":"","content":"Doesn't Mage Chroniclers Guide have a riff on this? I remember Captain America being a Frankenstein, which I love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T12:33:14-07:00","id":1128544,"title":"","content":"hmm, I know it sounds like a lot of superheroes are Deviants from their origin, but do they all define themselves entirely around how they relate to two or more people, organizations or ideals? I don't know. That said, I'm totally for all the Mutants to be Proximi","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T12:35:09-07:00","id":1128545,"title":"","content":"Well in the vein of the upcoming Netflix Defenders mini-series, I always saw:<ul><li>Daredevil as an Eshmaki Nemesis</li> <li>Jessica Jones as an Ogre Changeling of the Summer Court (manikin or truefriend kith, maybe?)</li> <li>Luke Cage as a Deviant</li> <li>Iron Fist as a Thyrsus of the Adamantine Arrow.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> ...otherwise for most of them it's like &quot;yup. Deviant. Almost all of 'em&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 08-13-2017, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T15:12:25-07:00","id":1128589,"title":"","content":"I think Blade might be a Dhampyr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T17:11:01-07:00","id":1128625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1128544#post1128544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmm, I know it sounds like a lot of superheroes are Deviants from their origin, but do they all define themselves entirely around how they relate to two or more people, organizations or ideals? I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, all was hyperbolic, although I think almost everyone can be stretched to be a Deviant. The obvious ones in the comic canon being the X-Men, Spider-Man, Hulk, Iron-Man post-Extermis, Weapon X, Cap, Winter Solider, Kamala Khan, Nick Fury, and Black Widow. In the timelines where everything can be traced back to attempts to recreate Cap's Supersoilder Serum (at least initially, that could have changed, I only read the early run and it has been some time), yes, I think pretty much everyone could be a Deviant. Which is not to say that Deviants are the only things they could be, but that their origins and struggles are a close match even if the exact story arcs aren't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1128544#post1128544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'm totally for all the Mutants to be Proximi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I love that idea too. It's not obvious, but it works, explains why all all of the Mutants have different powers, and provides set limits they can do. Now my only questions is what to do with Xavier and Magento. While I've toyed with the idea of uncoupling Magneto from the Holocaust and making him a Jew of a different nationality caught in a different genocide, I'm wondering if there may be a way write him up as a Beast, keep his origin story, and make him longer lived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T19:12:21-07:00","id":1128668,"title":"","content":"Saying this as a Jew, do not uncouple Magneto from the most interesting part of his character","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T19:22:05-07:00","id":1128671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1128625#post1128625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, all was hyperbolic, although I think almost everyone can be stretched to be a Deviant. The obvious ones in the comic canon being the X-Men, Spider-Man, Hulk, Iron-Man post-Extermis, Weapon X, Cap, Winter Solider, Kamala Khan, Nick Fury, and Black Widow. In the timelines where everything can be traced back to attempts to recreate Cap's Supersoilder Serum (at least initially, that could have changed, I only read the early run and it has been some time), yes, I think pretty much everyone could be a Deviant. Which is not to say that Deviants are the only things they could be, but that their origins and struggles are a close match even if the exact story arcs aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd prefer to get creative with the interpretations in order to avoid going all the same splat. Hulk, for example, also works as a Ghost Wolf or an Anakim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1128625#post1128625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I love that idea too. It's not obvious, but it works, explains why all all of the Mutants have different powers, and provides set limits they can do. Now my only questions is what to do with Xavier and Magento. While I've toyed with the idea of uncoupling Magneto from the Holocaust and making him a Jew of a different nationality caught in a different genocide, I'm wondering if there may be a way write him up as a Beast, keep his origin story, and make him longer lived.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw it as a Mysterium/Sliver Ladder Mystery cult split. But I admit that was something I had considered for a convention one-shot that never happened.Might return to it (and share) once more 2nd edition comes out.<br /> <br /> (It was a Suicide Squad/Thunderbolts style game; Company Zero team under a TF:V Hunter, a Slasher, Seemingless changeling, Proximi Magneto, Second Sight psychic and an Inferno Possessed.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T21:50:23-07:00","id":1128712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1128668#post1128668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying this as a Jew, do not uncouple Magneto from the most interesting part of his character</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't dare. The thought had crossed by mind to make him a Tutsi Jew caught in Rawandan Genocide and while I think it's an interesting idea, I'm not the person to write it. Hence, I need some way for him to be active and spry today while still having him live through WWII.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T02:03:40-07:00","id":1128735,"title":"","content":"Run in with a Time Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T02:11:02-07:00","id":1128736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1128712#post1128712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't dare. The thought had crossed by mind to make him a Tutsi Jew caught in Rawandan Genocide and while I think it's an interesting idea, I'm not the person to write it. Hence, I need some way for him to be active and spry today while still having him live through WWII.</div> </div> </div> </div>Put him on ice? It worked for Captain America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T03:32:12-07:00","id":1128745,"title":"","content":"If he's a Proximi, maybe he has some sort of age-defying spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T07:06:22-07:00","id":1128789,"title":"","content":"Marvel themselves will need to come up with something pretty soon. With Cap they can just keep increasing the time he was frozen, but magneto is just getting older and older...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T07:15:45-07:00","id":1128796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1128789#post1128789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marvel themselves will need to come up with something pretty soon. With Cap they can just keep increasing the time he was frozen, but magneto is just getting older and older...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mags has actually been de-aged once before I think","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T13:28:02-07:00","id":1128941,"title":"","content":"Doctor Strange is pretty clearly an Obrimos of the Ascended Adept Legacy, with a generous spread of dots in virtually all of the arcana (save perhaps Death, as that's the inferior arcanum for his path and I can't recall many examples from the comics of him using death or darkness spells). Not sure what Order he'd be; conventional wisdom would place him as either Adamantine Arrow (mystic protector of Earth and concerned with helping Sleepers) or Mysterium (collecting and preserving arcane knowledge and artifacts which might otherwise be lost).<br /> <br /> I've come up with concepts for Iron Man as a Moros mage and Spider-Man as a Skitterskulk changeling, so not too worried about making everybody with a science-y origin into a Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T16:40:03-07:00","id":1129015,"title":"","content":"Many splats come with a way to avoid Aging to a degree. Changelings, Werewolves and Beasts with high Supernatural Tolerance are longer lived. By all means, have Magneto be an Elemental Changeling or the like (albeit that does clash abit with the 'Giving up your Ego' Fluff).<br /> <br /> I like Daredevil as an Eshmaki Nemesis (who obviously has Relentless Hunter to keep up with this ridiculous Lifestyle, and Mimir's Wisdom to tell when people lie. Maybe something like Shadowed Soul, too.), but I also like to think of Kingpin as an Anakim Tyrant (with Limb from Limb reflecting his brutal blows and Alien Allure to explain his charisma). You could even make Power Man into an Anakim reluctant to feed his Hunger of Punishment (not the best fit, but workable, with Cyclopean Strength and Unbreakable, possibly Relentless Hunter). Hell, even The Immortal Iron Fist could be fluffed into being a Beast (Makara Nemesis, punishing all those trying to enter K'un Lun) who does not adhere to his Feeding Preference, a Dragon for a Horror and Limb from Limb Satiety Expenditure being his famous glowing fist, as well as Titanic Blow at the end of Season one. But then, I am biased like that.<br /> I like Spiderman as a Skitterskulk.<br /> Magik is obviously a Mastigos with high Space and some Mind, maybe some Spirits.<br /> I would like to see Collossus, but what would he be?<br /> <br /> There was a X-Men Microtemplate in the works, to represent stuff like the Wolverine.<br /> <br /> Any ideas for Uratha or Sin-Eaters?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T18:16:44-07:00","id":1129061,"title":"","content":"Besides the incredibly low-hanging fruit of Wolverine and Sabertooth? Hulk could be a very good fit as an Iron Master who really doesn't want to be a Werewolf and has a serious problem with Kuruth. Of all people, Doctor Strange may fit as a Werewolf if you don't make him a Mage, since his shtick as Sorcerer Supreme tends to be maintaining balance between the magical and physical work and banishing nasty spirits and demons.<br /> <br /> Deadpool is my most obvious pick for a Sin Eater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T19:10:58-07:00","id":1129083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1129061#post1129061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides the incredibly low-hanging fruit of Wolverine and Sabertooth? Hulk could be a very good fit as an Iron Master who really doesn't want to be a Werewolf and has a serious problem with Kuruth. Of all people, Doctor Strange may fit as a Werewolf if you don't make him a Mage, since his shtick as Sorcerer Supreme tends to be maintaining balance between the magical and physical work and banishing nasty spirits and demons.<br /> <br /> Deadpool is my most obvious pick for a Sin Eater.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually peg the Hulk as an Anakim Ravager who <i>really</i> doesn't like being a Beast.<br /> <br /> Deadpool as a Sin-Eater could work, but it's also possible that he's an Abmortal, seeing as the main description for an Abmortal is &quot;immortal serial killer&quot;, a bill that Wadey fits pretty well, all told.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T19:16:17-07:00","id":1129085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1129015#post1129015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas for Uratha or Sin-Eaters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh easy:<br /> <br /> All the Ghost Riders as Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> Much of their powers comes from the result of some type of vengeful spirit (in the case of Johnny Blaze and Danny Ketch) or a murderous ghost (Robbie Reyes) that come from some form of an Underworld that bonds to the mortal and giving them superpowers and exclusively dealing with supernatural threats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T19:45:30-07:00","id":1129088,"title":"","content":"Hulk could go many ways. If I were ever to do a Darths and Droids style webcomic for the MCU, he'd probably end up as a Demon who burns his cover between the Incredible Hulk and Avengers. I'm pretty sure that he was listed as inspiration for Deviant too. Promethean as well, especially if he tends to smash his way out of problems once Disquiet sets in. <br /> <br /> My rational for Deadpool was that the Geist would give Wade someone to talk to and he has legendary healing powers, but Abmortal is cool too. <br /> <br /> Given that <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?287815-The-Hearse-(A-Geist-The-Sin-Eaters-Manifestation)\" target=\"_blank\">The Hearse</a> pretty much exists just to play Ghost Rider, I can't believe I biffed on thinking of that. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T20:16:58-07:00","id":1129092,"title":"","content":"Lets see, I had Iron-Man as a Destroyer Saboteur demon who used to make occult equivalents to WMDs until he realised where god was sending his technology. His cover is a jerky billionaire, his demonic form is his armour, and he spends a lot of his time making gadgets. Thor was also a demon, though he was a Guardian Integrator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:18:39-07:00","id":1129311,"title":"","content":"Kraven could be either a Hero or a Huntsman, Venom could be obviously a Deviant, but how about going for Demon? Would change some things about the character(s), sure, but hey, It's a What if...? after all. Most of the Characters will experience a slight change in tone at least.<br /> Here are some of my takes on it:<br /> <br /> <br /> Galactus is a Rank 9 Spirit. Let's go with Idigam?<br /> Dr. Doom is a Mage with high Forces and Matter (and high Science, so you might alternatively go Genius), Obrimos imo.<br /> Punisher could be many things: A Hunter, or even a Slasher. Might go Beast, but I wouldn't recommend it. I like him as a Slasher, actually.<br /> Collossus could be a Beast or Deviant. I prefer Beast, which works well if seeing his Metallic mode as spending Satiety on Unbreakable. Deviant ain't out yet, after all ^^&quot;<br /> Antman could be a Genius? Otherwise a Moros with high Life and Matter?<br /> Black Panther is a Hunter in my Books, unique Conspiracy. His superior power comes from training, but also his suit and some sort of (let's call it what it is) coping. Making use of Elixirs made from herbs, so kinda like an Ascending Ones, and having special Relics (Suit, Claws etc.) like Aegis Kai Doru?<br /> Ultron is an Unfleshed Promethean, likely a Centimanus. ALthough Metalfleshed Elemental or Metalfleshed Fairest might work, too.<br /> Black Cat is an Eshmaki Collector, which is why she always returns to her nefarious ways.<br /> Loki is a Demon, what with his several different incarnations, illusions, fighting the boss deity, trying to carve out a kingdom for himself, and preferance for manipulation over brute force.<br /> Scarlet Witch is a Mage, as is Storm. Acanthus with high Prime and Obrimos with Forces and Matter, respectively? Storm might also work as a Beast (Ugallu Nemesis with Storm-Lashed, obviously. Also Wings of the Raptor - She'd be spending a lot of Satiety all the time, though. Mage fits way better)<br /> The Thing is a Tammuz Promethean.<br /> Mystique is a Mirrorskin Darkling.<br /> I like Wolverine and Sabertooth as Werewolves. Hulk could be refluffed into a Werewolf, though I like him as an Anakim who merges with his Horror whenever it get's ravenous ^^&quot;<br /> Johnny Storm is a Fireheart Fairest Changeling, and Groot is a Gargantuan Woodblood Elemental =P By this logic, Rocket Racoon could well be a Maker/Smith Beast Changeling with the Small Frame Merit (Although Wizened with an animalistic Kith like Hunterheart might fit too, on second thought. Prefer the first option, though.)<br /> Drax the Destroyer could be a Beast or an Ogre (prefering the Ogre here), Gamorra is... some sort of Changeling imo, (let's go with Bloodbrute Render Darkling, seems to reflect her past and current abilities well enough) and Star-Lord is a micro-template human Hunter? (No seriously, what is Star Lord in ChroD?)<br /> That would make the Guardians of the Galaxy a mixed troupe of mostly changelings. They fight Thanos and his people a lot, sooo... Thanos the Keeper, Ronin and company Huntsmen?<br /> Daimon Hellstorm is a Lucifuge Hunter.<br /> <br /> What's the Silver Surfer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 08-15-2017, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T12:50:54-07:00","id":1129369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1129311#post1129311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the Silver Surfer?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Werewolf: the Forsaken 2Ed&quot; gives Idigam &quot;Forge Herald&quot; ability. Now, I'm not saying... But I'm totally saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T13:51:05-07:00","id":1129406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1129369#post1129369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Werewolf: the Forsaken 2Ed&quot; gives Idigam &quot;Forge Herald&quot; ability. Now, I'm not saying... But I'm totally saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I have finally acquired WtF 2ed, I still haven't read it yet.<br /> I really, really should.<br /> Thanks for that, it made me chuckle! =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T14:12:03-07:00","id":1129419,"title":"","content":"Could probably fit En Sabah Nur as a high Primal Urge werewolf. He's basically a Pure version of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351\">Lycaon-Ur</a>. His ability to forge claimed justifies his Four Horsemen, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"