| <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:26:32-07:00","id":1129538,"title":"","content":"I think Rogue would be really hard to do. <br /> <br /> Nightcrawler, Changeling Shadowsoul. <br /> <br /> Collosus, Changeling Metalflesh Elemental. <br /> <br /> Woverine, Sabretooth, Wolf Blooded with a tell that grants regeneration. <br /> <br /> Emma Frost Magistos mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T20:26:02-07:00","id":1129615,"title":"","content":"There was a werewolf power in first edition that allowed them to steal the gifts of other supernaturals. Without eating them. So you could just do that, touching someone gives you a dread power equivalent of their gift, powered by Essence or Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T10:20:46-07:00","id":1129860,"title":"","content":"If Deadpool is a Sin-Eater, does that mean Cable is his Geist?<br /> <br /> Ghost Rider could be a Sin-Eater, as previously mentioned. But I can also see him as a Werewolf, with his motorcycle and chains being Fetishes. To keep the flaming skull visual, he could have Fetish Tattoos over his body that give bonus to use fire powers and intimidation when he shifts into Dalu form. Likely an Elodoth or Rahu of the Blood Talons.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of the Hulk as either a Deviant or a Zeka Promethean (Torment = HULK SMASH!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:48:27-07:00","id":1129962,"title":"","content":"Some more suggestions.<br /> <br /> Red Skull would be a Deviant, or an evil Changeling, I think.<br /> General Ross is a Hero, obsessed with The Hulk. At least, if you do not consider the Red Hulk Version, and make Hulk a Beast. Otherwise, he is a hyper-focused Hunter.<br /> Doctor Octopus is a Maker Wizened Changeling, or a Genius.<br /> Dormammu is a Spirit, Rank 9, as is the Phoenix Force.<br /> Bullseye is a Slasher.<br /> Juggernaut is a Tammuz Titan? Could be emulated to a degee by an Anakim Ravager with Titanic Blow and Advanced Giant.<br /> Sentinels are Metalflesh Huntsmen, or Pandorans? Prefer the former, since many X-Men come up Changelings for me.<br /> Sebastian Shaw is an Obrimos Mage going at it on his own.<br /> Professor X is a high-Mind Mage with some Space, so probably a (very affable and optimistic) Mastigos, or an Obrimos with a Legacy that helps with Mind. Also, Cerebro is an Artifact.<br /> Enchantress is obviously a Mage, but could also be some sort of Changeling I suppose.<br /> Dracula is a Vampire (duh), as is Hannibal King, who is most likely a High Humanity Gangrel. Blade is a Dhampir?<br /> Maestro could be an Incarnate.<br /> Surtur is a Changeling, Fireheart Ogre I suppose.<br /> Lizard is a Coldscale Beast, or a Were-reptile. Alternatively, a unique Claimed?<br /> Collector is most obviously a Collector Beast (Either Anakim or Makara), but could also be a Mysterium Mage.<br /> Sandman is a Sandharrowed Elemental, and Electro is also an Elemental.<br /> Thanos is either a True Fae or a High-Ranking Spirit. (True Fae would gel well with Gamora being a Changeling)<br /> Morbius is a Leechfinger Darkling (because I think that is both more fitting and interesting than going with just Vampire, although that could work with an appropriate Bloodline/Discipline, of course).<br /> Namor is some sort of Aquatic Changeling.<br /> Hit Monkey is a Beast Changeling. <br /> Squirrel Girl is ... a Rank 10 Spirit of Squirrels. Yes, you got that right. Not a Beast Changeling, but the most powerful category of spirits. Only this is capable of reflecting the awesome power that is calling and commanding squirrels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T08:49:39-07:00","id":1132636,"title":"","content":"I toyed with making a NWOD version of the MCU a while back this is what I came up with.<br /> <br /> Iron Man - Directly shaped by trauma involving being kidnapped, being forced to serve a cruel master and the fight for his freedom Tony Stark is a textbook Changeling. I'd say an Ogre Smith/Metalflesh although in this universe he's not wearing a suit so much as shedding his Mask.<br /> <br /> Whiplash - Another Smith Changeling (Seeming undetermined maybe Wizend?) who was condemned to his fate by Howard Stark in a deal with a True Fae many years ago.<br /> <br /> The Rest of the Iron Man movie villains (Iron Monger, Mandarin, Ten Rings, AIM, Killian, etc)- Titles of the same True Fae who made Tony.<br /> <br /> Warmachine - Tony's Fae-Touched best friend wearing token armour.<br /> <br /> Hulk - A Ghost Wolf who experienced his first change when exposed to lethal amounts of Gamma Radiation, which he mistakenly blames for his condition. Not truly understanding his nature has left him nearly constantly on edge of Death Rage.<br /> <br /> Abomination - A failed Cheiron Group experiment using the Hulk's genetic material.<br /> <br /> Red Skull - A Nosferatu member of the Ordo Dracul who entrenched himself within the Nazi warmachine.<br /> <br /> Captain America - This one is tricky but I went thematic and decided to go with a Davea. In this version he was embraced by Abraham Erskine, another member of Ordo Dracul who considered Red Skull's actions too monsterous and a Masquerade breach waiting to happen. So he approached Task Force Valkyrie with an offer to embrace a soldier of his choosing to combat the Red Skull. He picked Rogers on the basis that he didn't think such a pure hearted man could survive past the war as a Vampire so his own crimes could be forgiven. Unfortunately Steve is knocked into Toropor in the Arctic Ocean and is revived in modern nights.<br /> <br /> Hydra - A splinter group from the Ordo than espouses genocidal transhumanism. Seeking to make better Vampires by making better humans through horrific experimentation.<br /> <br /> Thor - Centuries ago a handful of Arisen made their way to Scandinavia and shaped the local religion becoming the source of Norse mythology. Thor (originally Tor but Vikings added an H and it stuck) has since relocated to America. I know very little about Mummy so the entries for Thor characters may be total BS.<br /> <br /> Loki - Another Arisen who went to Scandinavia and later American. I don't really know enough about Mummy to justify his issues with his brother but I'm sure there is something.<br /> <br /> Jane Foster - A Null Mysteries Hunter who had infiltrated Thor's cult in order to study him.<br /> <br /> Black Widow, Hawkeye, Nick Fury, Coulson, SHIELD in General - More or less unchanged but they are part of Task Force Valkyrie now<br /> <br /> Thanos - Since he has yet to actually do anything I just up and replaced him with the God Machine. The Infinity Stones are long lost pieces of Infrastructure it has begun seeking out for mysterious inscrupulous reasons.<br /> <br /> Falcon - Keeping with the Cap as Vampire theme Falcon is a Gangrel soldier who was embraced upon returning from Afghanistan. He's far lower Blood Potency than Cap though. He's kind of involved with the DC area Carpathians but only because they let him run a support group for vets who's lives were messed up by the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Winter Soldier - Cap's war time buddy kept alive, brainwashed and in his physical prime as a Ghoul by surviving Hydra cells as an assassin.<br /> <br /> Malekith - A True Fae who was an issue for the Scandinavian Arisen.<br /> <br /> Guardians of the Galaxy - Starlord, Gamora and Rocket all have backstories of being abducted and changed by aliens and Draxx has a similar backstory in the comics. So they are now The Guardians of the Hedge a motley of Changelings. Groot is a hobgoblin bound to Rocket.<br /> <br /> Yondu - A former privateer who helped abduct Starlord as a kid.<br /> <br /> Nebula - An active Privateer for Ronan.<br /> <br /> Ronan - Gamora and Draxx's Keeper, currently involved with the God Machine to seek an Infinity Stone.<br /> <br /> Ultron and Vision - Unfleshed Prometheans<br /> <br /> Quicksilver and Wanda - Mages who were brought to Awakening by horrific experiments by Hydra.<br /> <br /> Doctor Strange and related Magical characters - Adamantite Arrow Mages<br /> <br /> Dormanu - An incredibly high rank Inferno demon.<br /> <br /> Ego - Starlord's Keeper<br /> <br /> Vulture - A Union Hunter who started reverse engineering some TFV tech.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what to make of Spider-Man or Ant-Man.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T11:06:04-07:00","id":1132707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1132636#post1132636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iron Man - Directly shaped by trauma involving being kidnapped, being forced to serve a cruel master and the fight for his freedom Tony Stark is a textbook Changeling. I'd say an Ogre Smith/Metalflesh although in this universe he's not wearing a suit so much as shedding his Mask.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually go with Wizened. He has the lingering physical maladies, as well as having been taken for his skills, rather than brute muscle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hulk - A Ghost Wolf who experienced his first change when exposed to lethal amounts of Gamma Radiation, which he mistakenly blames for his condition. Not truly understanding his nature has left him nearly constantly on edge of Death Rage. </div> </div> </div>A possibility. The rage fits, but the Hulk isn't very canine. I'd place him as an Anakim Tyrant, or possibly a Zeka made from Banner's body with the Residual Memories merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Captain America - This one is tricky but I went thematic and decided to go with a Davea. In this version he was embraced by Abraham Erskine, another member of Ordo Dracul who considered Red Skull's actions too monsterous and a Masquerade breach waiting to happen. So he approached Task Force Valkyrie with an offer to embrace a soldier of his choosing to combat the Red Skull. He picked Rogers on the basis that he didn't think such a pure hearted man could survive past the war as a Vampire so his own crimes could be forgiven. Unfortunately Steve is knocked into Toropor in the Arctic Ocean and is revived in modern nights. </div> </div> </div>That seems like an odd choice. Nothing about Captain America really says &quot;vampire.&quot; Given that his enhanced status was the result of a super-serum, I would say Deviant, but he doesn't really have anything resembling a Scar. Maybe he has some augmentation from Cheiron?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thor - Centuries ago a handful of Arisen made their way to Scandinavia and shaped the local religion becoming the source of Norse mythology. Thor (originally Tor but Vikings added an H and it stuck) has since relocated to America. I know very little about Mummy so the entries for Thor characters may be total BS. </div> </div> </div>Thor doesn't really fit for a Mummy in my opinion. He can move about pretty much as he pleases, he's not tethered to any greater force, and he's not prone to memory loss, nor does he really do most of the miraculous/terrifying things Mummies do other than the lightning. I'd actually put the Asgardians as the residents of an Emanation Realm, with Loki and Odin probably qualifying as Awakened, and possibly Thor himself. I'm still waiting on Ragnarok, though, so that might change.[/quote]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanos - Since he has yet to actually do anything I just up and replaced him with the God Machine. The Infinity Stones are long lost pieces of Infrastructure it has begun seeking out for mysterious inscrupulous reasons. </div> </div> </div>Thanos, I would place as a Moros Archmage. The Infinity Stones are a tool he intend to use to ascend by uniting himself with the Death Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ronan - Gamora and Draxx's Keeper, currently involved with the God Machine to seek an Infinity Stone. </div> </div> </div>Actually, Thanos would be Gamora's keeper, if he were True Fae annd Gamora a Changeling. Gamora and Nebula were both his adopted daughters from two different planets he annihilated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quicksilver and Wanda - Mages who were brought to Awakening by horrific experiments by Hydra. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call them Awakened. At most, I'd call them Proximi, although Wanda might be on her way to Awakening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dormanu - An incredibly high rank Inferno demon. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that works. Dormammu is defined (in the MCU) by coming from a plane of existence without time. That sounds more consistent with a Time-deficient plane of Abaddon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure what to make of Spider-Man or Ant-Man. </div> </div> </div>Spidey I would place as a Deviant, who keeps his powers deliberately low-key in order to avoid getting too spider-y (Google &quot;man-spider&quot;, you'll know what I'm talking about.).<br /> <br /> Ant-Man, I'd say he's a Hunter, with a custome Endowment that makes up his suit.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> I'd place the Watcher as an Archmage, or possibly a Rank-8 ephemeral being of uncertain origin. The Living Tribunal is Rank 9, and the One Above All is likely Rank 10, seeing as he's, well, &quot;Above All,&quot; and you can't really get more &quot;above all&quot; than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T11:56:59-07:00","id":1132732,"title":"","content":"Spider-man could easily be portrayed as an azlu, or at least someone with an azlu soul shard. Otherwise, really, ridden or low-level claiming seems the best. The Predators book practically has a picture of Spider-man in it.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/FwYWHqh.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-22-2017, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T12:08:29-07:00","id":1132738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1132732#post1132732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spider-man could easily be portrayed as an azlu, or at least someone with an azlu soul shard. Otherwise, really, ridden or low-level claiming seems the best. The Predators book practically has a picture of Spider-man in it.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/FwYWHqh.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I didn't think about Azlu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:07:47-07:00","id":1132759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1132707#post1132707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd actually go with Wizened. He has the lingering physical maladies, as well as having been taken for his skills, rather than brute muscle.<br /> <br /> A possibility. The rage fits, but the Hulk isn't very canine. I'd place him as an Anakim Tyrant, or possibly a Zeka made from Banner's body with the Residual Memories merit.<br /> <br /> That seems like an odd choice. Nothing about Captain America really says &quot;vampire.&quot; Given that his enhanced status was the result of a super-serum, I would say Deviant, but he doesn't really have anything resembling a Scar. Maybe he has some augmentation from Cheiron?<br /> <br /> Spidey I would place as a Deviant, who keeps his powers deliberately low-key in order to avoid getting too spider-y (Google &quot;man-spider&quot;, you'll know what I'm talking about.).<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooh, I really like the Wizened Changeling idea!<br /> Not nearly as much as the Zeka Banner, though! Sure, he doesn't actually grow green and big as written, but it's not hard to fluff a transmutation to fit that. And with his focus on &quot;Leave me alone&quot;, I'd peck him as a Cuprum.<br /> How about having Cap be a High-Integrity Hero and Red Skull a particularly nasty Beast who tries to achieve Inheritance via Nazis/Hydra?<br /> <br /> Heh, completely forgot about ManSpider. Huh. That would make him a far better Deviant then Beast. (Nemesis would still work, though, imo. Family would be a tad harder to pick.)<br /> <br /> Btw, weren't Azlu antagonistic/evil though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:10:32-07:00","id":1132760,"title":"","content":"Well, they don't like werewolves. But individually they can vary. Plus as we have Azlu/Werewolf hybrids you could probably get more variation through other ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T14:57:36-07:00","id":1132810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1132760#post1132760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they don't like werewolves. But individually they can vary. Plus as we have Azlu/Werewolf hybrids you could probably get more variation through other ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh, that went somehow completly past me! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T15:45:22-07:00","id":1132824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1132759#post1132759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooooh, I really like the Wizened Changeling idea!<br /> Not nearly as much as the Zeka Banner, though! Sure, he doesn't actually grow green and big as written, but it's not hard to fluff a transmutation to fit that. And with his focus on &quot;Leave me alone&quot;, I'd peck him as a Cuprum.<br /> How about having Cap be a High-Integrity Hero and Red Skull a particularly nasty Beast who tries to achieve Inheritance via Nazis/Hydra?<br /> <br /> Heh, completely forgot about ManSpider. Huh. That would make him a far better Deviant then Beast. (Nemesis would still work, though, imo. Family would be a tad harder to pick.)<br /> <br /> Btw, weren't Azlu antagonistic/evil though?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to pick a family, it'd be either Ugallu (given his propensity for swinging down from above), or possibly Eshmaki if we take his proclivity for sneaking into account. <i>Maybe</i> Namtaru if we focus on the Spider in Spider-Man.<br /> <br /> Though, a proper Were-spider template would also be a way to do it, especially if you bring in the Spider-Totem mythology and consider the Spider Totem to be a powerful spirit analogous to Father Wolf. I know Spinner-Kin were a thing, but a lot of people don't like Changing Breeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 08-22-2017, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T21:59:01-07:00","id":1133667,"title":"","content":"Stepping away from &quot;Cap as a Vamp&quot;, Captain America/Steve Rogers, Bucky and to a degree Wolverine/James 'Logan' Howlet work as Arisen as far as themes go. (Power is way off but such differences make the interpretations more interesting IMHO). Loss of control, missing memories, out of time...<br /> <br /> Heck the vita-ray/super-serum could have been a twice-born rite. Even goes as far as the 'alignment' change in Secret Empire: he is recalling a different descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T22:58:08-07:00","id":1133679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1133667#post1133667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stepping away from &quot;Cap as a Vamp&quot;, Captain America/Steve Rogers, Bucky and to a degree Wolverine/James 'Logan' Howlet work as Arisen as far as themes go. (Power is way off but such differences make the interpretations more interesting IMHO). Loss of control, missing memories, out of time...<br /> <br /> Heck the vita-ray/super-serum could have been a twice-born rite. Even goes as far as the 'alignment' change in Secret Empire: he is recalling a different descent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Logan is always active though, no noticeable down-time.<br /> <br /> Bucky and Cap - interesting idea. Would need to work out why the power level is so low, but otherwise...<br /> That would, however, make Hydra a Bucky cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T02:00:28-07:00","id":1133707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1133679#post1133679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. Logan is always active though, no noticeable down-time.<br /> <br /> Bucky and Cap - interesting idea. Would need to work out why the power level is so low, but otherwise...<br /> That would, however, make Hydra a Bucky cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a group that eliminated his original cult and learned the 'waking rite'. Remember, it is possible for a cult to boss around its Arisen. If your cult is dead and someone else learns how to wake you...you've been recruited. It's not like you remember what your cult is like when you first wake later.<br /> As for the power level...modern day is the low point of their descents. On the other hand, I am less fussed about it. anyway. The differences are interesting to me.<br /> <br /> As for Logan...Promethean also sort of works, though wolfblooded/Uratha is still the best mechanical model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T02:28:06-07:00","id":1133710,"title":"","content":"A Wolf-Blooded Deviant. While most of his powers comes from himself, he definitely have a Deviant style backstory with the Weapon X program.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T21:03:14-07:00","id":1134739,"title":"","content":"Thor could also work as a Beast, I think. I'd say an Anakim Nemesis, with Storm-Lashed, Cyclopean Strength, and Titanic Blow. His Horror is just himself, grown to giant size and surrounded by an eternal maelstrom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T23:18:39-07:00","id":1209923,"title":"","content":"Thanks to the Skin Deep Atavism, it is now far easier to represent beings such as Wolverine and the Hulk as Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T08:04:02-07:00","id":1210028,"title":"","content":"I've played around with the idea of Cap as a Promethean, actually. There are a couple of great essays floating around Tumblr about how the Captain America origin story is a sci-fi reworking of the Golem of Prague. Actual CoD!Cap would have to be an Extempore, though, and I'm not really sure what kind of Disquiet effects make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T08:37:00-07:00","id":1210039,"title":"","content":"People have floated around the idea of Ascended Mummy Cap. It could be one of the Sybarises that make people worship you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T20:06:18-07:00","id":1210247,"title":"","content":"Going purely by MCU portrayal;<br /> <br /> Ultron: Stannum Promethean who spends most of the last part of the movie in his &quot;Destructive&quot; Torment after losing his progeny, Vision.<br /> <br /> Dr. Strange: Mysterium Obrimos, since at the end he seems more interested in researching magic than being directly proactive.<br /> <br /> Hela: Incarnate Anakim drawing power from her Myth as the Executioner of Gods.<br /> <br /> Ego: Powerful idigam who has Coalesced around the concept of Growth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T21:49:42-07:00","id":1210280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128540-what-if-the-marvel-universe?p=1210247#post1210247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dr. Strange: Mysterium Obrimos, since at the end he seems more interested in researching magic than being directly proactive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would point Strange as more 'healer camp' Adamantine Arrow. He want to excel in what he do, he want's to literally heal the world - and in the end, he does gladly fight the Darkness - only in smart, not brutish way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T21:52:41-07:00","id":1212535,"title":"","content":"I don't like the idea of the Fantastic Four being different types of supernatural creatures--I vote for them all being the same kind of thing, and for me the obvious choice is a Krewe of Sin-Eaters. They rocketed off into space, died by cosmic radiation or somesuch, and bonded with some elemental Geister to make it back to ground. Going based on nWoD rules (because we haven't got CoD rules for Sin-Eaters yet), I'd say they must all have taken Caul manifestations with one elemental Key apiece.<br /> <br /> I agree with the poster who said that Black Panther should be a Hunter, but I reckon some arm of the Ascendant Order rather than a custom conspiracy. His powers, such as they are, come from eating the sacred heart-shaped herb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","user":"gscrap","date":". 04-28-2018, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T06:45:43-07:00","id":1213043,"title":"","content":"Coming from the MCU...spoilers for Infinity War.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].ge